the united states has announced a  diplomatic boycott of the beijing winter  olympics over china's human rights  record the measure should not impact u.s  athletes competing in the games next  year but china's government has  threatened to take countermeasures  the snow making machines are working  full blast as the chinese test their  winter venues weeks before the calendar  says it's winter but less than two  months before the start of the 2022  winter games  athletes around the world have been  sharpening their skills even as human  rights advocates call for a total  boycott of the games pointing to the  internment camps in xinjiang province  where they say china has allegedly  detained up to a million muslim uyghurs  against their will  the white house finally decided on a  softer approach u.s athletes should  compete u.s diplomats should stay home  the biden administration will not send  any diplomatic or official  representation to the beijing 2022  winter olympics and paralympic games  given the pierre scenes ongoing genocide  and crimes against  humanity in xinjiang and other human  rights abuses  the chinese foreign ministry knew this  might be coming and earlier in the day  tried to preempt the diplomatic boycott  without being invited  american politicians keep hyping the  so-called diplomatic boycott of the  beijing winter olympics which are purely  wishful thinking and grandstanding  political manipulation is a blatant  insult of the spirit of the olympic  charter and an outright political  provocation  the dispatching of high-level  delegations to each olympics and  paralympics is a tradition for the u.s  and other leading nations first lady  jill biden attended the tokyo games this  summer  u.s delegation seats will be empty this  february though china is certain to say  they were never invited anyway  our washington correspondent carolina  chamoy has been looking into whether  other countries are planning a similar  boycott  that is precisely what the united states  would like to see secretary of state  anthony blinken he said that the u.s has  been consulting with allies and partners  on a shared approach to the beijing  games because of their concern about  china's human rights record um and the  chief of the european union's diplomatic  service here in washington dc he said  last week after some meetings with u.s  officials that it was important to keep  up pressure on china indeed over the  abuses in xinjiang but that anybody  caught was in the domain and if the the  hands of each country and not uh it was  not a common position of the european  union on foreign policy and chinese  state media have said that beijing does  not intend to invite western politicians  who have threatened a boycott actually  russian president vladimir putin he is  the only leader of a major country who  has accepted china's invitation to  attend these games
 

